<object-publication class="lab wide" aria-label="Publish two files together">
  <div class="lab-heading"><span class="eyebrow">Interactive experiment</span><span class="lab-number">01</span></div>
  <h3>Can a reader see half an export?</h3>
  <div class="lab-introduction">
    <p>A shop exports two files for its blue mug: a price and a stock count. Generation A says <strong>20 credits, 4 in stock</strong>. Generation B says <strong>24 credits, 8 in stock</strong>. Both files must come from the same generation.</p>
    <p class="try-this">Start with <strong>Replace the files</strong> and choose <strong>Next write</strong> once. Inspect what a reader would get at that moment. Then reset, choose <strong>Publish a manifest</strong>, and step through all three writes. When does the reader move from A to B?</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-controls" data-object-controls hidden>
    <p class="lab-area-label">Controls</p>
    <div class="control-line"><label>Publication method <select data-object-mode><option value="overwrite">Replace the files</option><option value="manifest">Publish a manifest</option></select></label></div>
    <div class="control-line"><button data-object-next>Next write</button><button data-object-reset>Reset</button><span data-object-step>Before any writes</span></div>
    <p class="control-note">Changing the method starts again from generation A. The reader shown below starts a fresh read after each step.</p>
  </div>
  <div class="lab-output paper-surface">
    <p class="lab-area-label">Result <span>What a reader gets now</span></p>
    <p data-object-action>No writes yet.</p>
    <div class="object-reader-grid"><div><span>Price file</span><strong data-object-price>20 credits</strong><small data-object-price-generation>Generation A</small></div><div><span>Stock file</span><strong data-object-stock>4 in stock</strong><small data-object-stock-generation>Generation A</small></div></div>
    <p class="object-pointer" data-object-pointer>Reader requests prices.json and stock.json directly.</p>
    <p data-object-result role="status" aria-live="polite">The reader gets generation A: price 20 credits and stock 4. The two files belong to the same export.</p>
  </div>
  <details class="model-note"><summary>What this model leaves out</summary><p>One writer, two complete files, and a reader starting between successful writes. No network failures, caches, permissions, multipart uploads, or garbage collection. The manifest method requires immutable generation files and readers that fetch the manifest once per export. It does not give arbitrary multi-object transactions. Credits are invented example prices.</p></details>
  <noscript><p>Replacing the price before the stock exposes generation B's price with generation A's stock. Uploading both B files under new names and then publishing their manifest keeps readers on A until the complete B export is ready.</p></noscript>
</object-publication>
<style>
  .object-reader-grid { display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem;margin:1.4rem 0; }
  .object-reader-grid > div { border-block:1px solid var(--color-rule-strong);padding:1rem .7rem; }
  .object-reader-grid span,.object-reader-grid small { display:block;font-size:.8rem;color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .object-reader-grid strong { display:block;font:1.7rem var(--font-serif);margin:.4rem 0; }
  .object-pointer { border-left:3px solid var(--gold);padding-left:.8rem;font-size:.8rem; }
  @media(max-width:420px) { .object-reader-grid { gap:.5rem; }.object-reader-grid strong { font-size:1.35rem; } }
</style>
<script>
  import { publicationState } from '../../lib/explainers/object-publication.mjs';
  class ObjectPublication extends HTMLElement {
    connectedCallback() {
      if (this.dataset.ready) return;
      this.dataset.ready='true';
      let mode='overwrite', step=0;
      const node=(name:string)=>this.querySelector<HTMLElement>(`[data-object-${name}]`)!;
      const render=()=>{
        const state=publicationState(mode,step);
        node('price').textContent=`${state.price} credits`;
        node('stock').textContent=`${state.stock} in stock`;
        node('price-generation').textContent=`Generation ${state.priceGeneration}`;
        node('stock-generation').textContent=`Generation ${state.stockGeneration}`;
        node('action').textContent=state.action;
        node('result').textContent=state.summary;
        node('pointer').textContent=mode==='manifest'
          ? `Manifest points to ${state.pointer}/prices.json and ${state.pointer}/stock.json. ${state.uploaded} of 2 generation-B files uploaded.`
          : 'Reader requests prices.json and stock.json directly.';
        const lastStep=mode==='manifest'?3:2;
        node('step').textContent=step===0?'Before any writes':`Step ${step} of ${lastStep}`;
        (node('next') as HTMLButtonElement).disabled=step===lastStep;
      };
      node('controls').hidden=false;
      node('mode').addEventListener('change',event=>{mode=(event.target as HTMLSelectElement).value;step=0;render();});
      node('next').addEventListener('click',()=>{step=Math.min(mode==='manifest'?3:2,step+1);render();});
      node('reset').addEventListener('click',()=>{step=0;render();});
    }
  }
  if(!customElements.get('object-publication'))customElements.define('object-publication',ObjectPublication);
</script>
